#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:18
msgid "2. Intrusion Alert System with Blynk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:28
msgid "This project demonstrate a simple home intrusion detection system using a passive infrared (PIR) sensor (HC-SR501). When the system is set to 'Away' mode through the Blynk app, the PIR sensor monitors for motion. Any detected movement triggers a notification on the Blynk app, alerting the user of potential intrusion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:33
msgid "1. Build the Circuit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:37
msgid "The module draws a high current at start-up, so make sure the 9 V battery or an external power supply is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:44
msgid ":ref:`cpn_uno`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:45
msgid ":ref:`cpn_espc201`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:46
msgid ":ref:`cpn_pir_motion`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:50
msgid "2. Configure Blynk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:54
msgid "The template and the device were created once in :ref:`c201_iot_blynk_start`. Every project adds its datastreams to that **same** template, so each project occupies its own range of virtual pins. This project uses **V1** and **V2**. Nothing here changes the device token, so the sketch keeps working as it is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:59
msgid "**There are two things to tell the cloud, and one of them is worth two datastreams.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:61
msgid "``away_mode`` - the switch you flip on your way out of the house."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:62
msgid "``current_status`` - a line of text the board writes back, so you can see what it is doing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:64
msgid "**Add the datastreams**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:66
msgid "Open **Developer Zone** -> **My Templates**, click **Ultimate Sensor Kit**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:71
msgid "Click **Edit** to open the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:76
msgid "Click **Datastreams**, then **Create New**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:81
msgid "Create the first datastream:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:83
msgid "**DATASTREAM NAME**: ``away_mode``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:84
msgid "**DISPLAY NAME**: ``Away Mode``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:85
msgid "**VIRTUAL PIN**: ``V1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:86
msgid "**DATA TYPE**: **Integer**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:87
msgid "**MIN** ``0``, **MAX** ``1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:91
msgid "An integer with a range of 0..1 is the usual way to model a switch: ``1`` means the alarm is armed, ``0`` means it is off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:97
msgid "Click **Create New** again for the second datastream:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:99
msgid "**DATASTREAM NAME**: ``current_status``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:100
msgid "**DISPLAY NAME**: ``Current Status``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:101
msgid "**VIRTUAL PIN**: ``V2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:102
msgid "**DATA TYPE**: **String**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:106
msgid "A **String** holds text. The board sends lines such as ``Detecting signs of intrusion...`` or ``Somebody in your house!``, which a Label widget can show as is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:112
msgid "The list now shows both datastreams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:117
msgid "**Add the event**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:119
msgid "An event is what turns a sensor reading into a notification on your phone. Without it the alarm only changes a label - nobody notices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:122
msgid "Open **Events & notifications**, then click **Create Event**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:127
msgid "Set **EVENT CODE** to ``intrusion_detected``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:131
msgid "Type it exactly like this. The sketch calls ``Blynk.logEvent(\"intrusion_detected\")``, and any other spelling silently does nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:137
msgid "Turn the notification on and choose where it should go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:142
msgid "**Add the web dashboard**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:144
msgid "The dashboard is the part you look at. Two widgets are enough here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:146
msgid "Click **Dashboard**, then **Add Widget**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:151
msgid "Drag a **Label** widget onto the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:156
msgid "Add a **Switch** widget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:161
msgid "Click the three dots in the corner of the **Label** and choose **Settings**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:163
msgid "Set **Datastream** to ``Current Status (V2)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:169
msgid "Do the same for the **Switch**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:171
msgid "Set **Datastream** to ``Away Mode (V1)``, **ON LABEL** ``away home`` and **OFF LABEL** ``at home``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:176
msgid "Click **Save**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:183
msgid "3. Run the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:185
msgid "Open the ``02-Intrusion_alert_system.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\wifi\\02-Intrusion_alert_system``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:187
msgid "The three Blynk lines are the ones you copied in the Get Started chapter. Leave them as they are - the device is already created, so only the Wi-Fi settings differ between projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:197
msgid "Type the name and the password of your own Wi-Fi network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:204
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:206
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. When the board reaches the cloud the log ends with ``Ready``. Every time you flip the switch in the app, a line appears here - that is how you know the two are talking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:213
msgid "Now flip the switch to **away home** and wave your hand in front of the PIR sensor. The label on the dashboard changes to ``Somebody in your house! Please check!`` and your phone shows a notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:220
msgid "To use Blynk on a phone, see :ref:`blynk_mobile`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:223
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:225
msgid "**Blynk account and libraries**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:227
msgid "The first three lines say which Blynk device this board belongs to. They come from the device page and are identical in every project of the kit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:241
msgid "**The serial port that talks to the module**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:243
msgid "The ESPC2-01 is not running your sketch - it works as a modem that answers AT commands. On the R4 it sits on D0/D1, which is ``Serial1``, a hardware port, so 115200 works without bit errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:253
msgid "**PIR pin and the two state variables**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:264
msgid "``state`` is what makes the next section possible: comparing the new reading with the old one tells you the moment somebody walks past, instead of \"there is a person\" a hundred times. ``awayHomeMode`` is the answer to \"am I at home or not\" - the alarm only reacts when it is ``1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:269
msgid "**espModuleInit() - wake the module up first**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:271
msgid "The module needs about a second to boot, and it prints its start-up log on the very wire the sketch is about to use. Send commands too early and the replies get tangled with that log. This function waits for the word ``ready``, then sends ``ATE0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:292
msgid "``ATE0`` turns the echo off. With echo on, every reply starts with the command you just sent, and Blynk reads that line as garbage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:295
msgid "**setup()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:313
msgid "``timer.setInterval(1000L, myTimerEvent)`` calls the function once per second. Change that number to check the sensor more or less often."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:316
msgid "**loop()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:325
msgid "``Blynk.run()`` keeps the connection alive, ``timer.run()`` fires the scheduled function. Nothing here may block, or the cloud drops the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:328
msgid "**BLYNK_CONNECTED() and BLYNK_WRITE(V1)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:341
msgid "``BLYNK_CONNECTED()`` runs every time the board reaches the server - including after a power cut. ``Blynk.syncVirtual(V1)`` asks for the current switch position, so a board that restarted at midnight still knows that you left the house."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:345
msgid "``BLYNK_WRITE(V1)`` runs whenever the switch in the app is moved. ``param.asInt()`` is the new value, ``1`` or ``0``, and the reply goes straight back to the label on datastream **V2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:349
msgid "**sendData() - react to the edge, not the level**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:365
msgid "``rising`` is true only on the step from ``LOW`` to ``HIGH`` - the moment the sensor reacts. Without it the sketch would send a message every second for as long as someone stands there, which burns through the Blynk quota in minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:368
msgid "``millis() - lastAlert > 5000`` keeps two alerts at least five seconds apart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:369
msgid "``Blynk.virtualWrite(V2, ...)`` writes the text the label widget displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/02-iot_Intrusion_alert_system.rst:370
msgid "``Blynk.logEvent(\"intrusion_detected\")`` sends the event that pops the notification up. The name must match the **EVENT CODE** you created, character for character."
msgstr ""
